Vendored files:

  query_validator.py
      From app/proxy/query_validator.py. Validates a GraphQL query against the
      Tableau Metadata API schema and returns a list of error strings.
      MODIFICATIONS:
        - imports rebased from the upstream `proxy` package to
          `estate_scan.vendor`;
        - the optional comprehensive layer (schema_validator + the ~6.9 MB
          introspection dump) and the per-tenant runtime rules are not vendored,
          so both optional imports resolve absent and the module runs its
          self-contained structural checks plus the whitelist checks. This is the
          graceful degradation the upstream try/except already provides.
      The validation logic itself is unmodified.

  types-and-filters.md
      From app/static/schema/types-and-filters.md. The introspected type,
      lineage, and filter-field reference from which query_validator builds its
      whitelists. Unmodified.

  schema_loader.py
      NOT from upstream. A minimal shim we wrote to feed query_validator the one
      attribute it reads (`_types_and_filters`), loading only types-and-filters.md.

Why vendored rather than depended-on: the upstream modules are coupled to a Flask
application (tenant DB, settings, logger) and pin assumptions we replace (API
version, Cloud-only TLS). We reuse the hard-won query-validation knowledge, not
the application. See 05-metadata-explorer-reuse.md sections 2 and 7.3.
